# scroll_cost.pixels -- frozen frame-hash baseline for tests/scroll_cost_harness.ast (v2.7).
# Generated by running scroll_cost_harness under aster-fixed (md5 86234516...),
# 2026-11-15: SCROLLHASH s=0 1773845912, s=1 -1823807559 (twice in one
# run, twice across runs, deterministic; output byte-identical).
# The hashes are the post-drag blit frames (off=180); PIXELCHECK
# asserts each equals a forced full repaint in the same run.
# v2.7 fixed two scroll-jank root causes, both pinned here by the
# test's per-step assertions (build 0, paint 1, miss/evict 0,
# drag blit 5/6, fling blit >= 4/6):
# (1) fb_cmds_ok's backward scan was blocked by a header text box's
# 6 px empty line-height graze (why=5), so the blit never engaged;
# (2) the 32-entry glyph cache thrashed on every screen (probe 62,
# Fonts tab ~90 distinct glyphs), re-rasterizing every visible glyph
# per frame. Cache is now 128 entries.
# Re-pin only when the scene or the rendering legitimately changes.
SCROLLHASH s=0 1773845912
SCROLLHASH s=1 -1823807559
